---
description: Parse -chat, -doc, and -feat:name flags; write per-prompt feature docs under doc/feats/
alwaysApply: true
---

# Prompt flags

Scan the **current user message** for these flags before doing anything else. Strip them from the task. They may appear anywhere, combined, and `-docs` is an alias for `-doc`.

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-chat` | Normal agent work. Do **not** write files under `doc/`. |
| `-doc` / `-docs` | After the work is done, write one new markdown file for this prompt. |
| `-feat:<name>` | Feature slug (folder under `doc/feats/`). Also writes a doc, same as `-doc`. |

Default when no flags: `-chat`.

## Feature folder

- Path: `doc/feats/<feature-slug>/`
- Slug: lowercase kebab-case (`quote-search`). From `-feat:<name>` when present.
- `-doc` **without** `-feat:`: infer a short slug from the prompt (noun of the work). Reuse an existing folder if the name clearly matches; otherwise create a new one.
- `-feat:` writes a new prompt file in that feature folder (creates the folder if needed).
- `-chat` wins over `-doc` / `-feat` for documentation: do the work, skip the doc file.
- Never overwrite a previous prompt file. Each documented prompt = one new file.

## Doc file name

`doc/feats/<feature-slug>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<HHMM>-<short-slug>.md`

Use the real date/time. `short-slug` is 3–6 kebab words from the prompt. If that path exists, append `-2`, `-3`, …

Create `doc/feats/` and the feature folder as needed. Do not add an index unless asked.

## When to write

Write the doc **after** the implementation (or after the answer, if there was no code). Write it when `-doc` / `-docs` or `-feat:` is present, unless `-chat` is also present.

Fill the template from what actually happened. Omit empty optional sections.

```markdown
# <Feature Title> — <Prompt Title>

**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM
**Feature:** `<feature-slug>`
**Flags:** <flags used>
**Prompt:** <user message with flags stripped>

## Summary

<2–4 sentences: what changed and why.>

## What was made

- <user-visible outcome>
- <files created / updated / deleted — paths only>

## How it was made

- <approach and key decisions>
- <patterns, APIs, or commands used>
- <tests or checks run, or none>

## Follow-ups

- <optional next steps; omit section if none>
```
